A||||8||fldevel||ticking sound||||1||
Z||000000||fldevel||01-03-2000||03:13 PM||||i just bought a 85 fiero GT and it runs great ..looks great...drives great ..but there is a little ticking sound comeing from the engine ...is this normal or should i look into it further ?||||reg||1
Z||000001||ChadMan||01-03-2000||03:49 PM||||It's probably a leaky exhaust manifold or manifold gasket.  This ticking would be barely audible at idle, but much louder under moderate to heavy acceleration.  Look for sooty deposits around the gaskets - that's another clue.<P>I wonder how many V6 Fieros have been sold because their owners heard that ticking and thought the engine was getting ready to blow, when it was just an exhaust leak?  (I got one cheap because of this very problem.)||||reg||1
Z||000002||sluppy123||01-03-2000||03:50 PM||||Check for an exhaust leak, cracked or broken manifolds are common on the V-6<P>-Brian||||reg||1
Z||000003||DRH||01-03-2000||03:52 PM||||Welcome to Fiero ownership and this Forum!<P>It's a little hard to diagnose sounds by a written description. You might try listening thru a long piece of hose or pipe to try to get a more exact location of the origin of the sound. Also, is it more noticable cold, hot, at idle, on acceleration, etc.<P>A very common cause of a "ticking" sound on a V6 Fiero is a cracked exhaust manifold or a bad exhaust manifold gasket. It is usually the front one. A cracked manifold may be hard to see on the car but you should be able to tell by listening carefully from above and below. If the manifold is cracked, you should plan on fixing it eventually... it will only get worse and could eventually cause more major problems.<P>David.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||DXR_DAD||01-03-2000||05:32 PM||||Welcome to the "Little Plastic Toy Fourm"<BR>and to the fiero!!<P>This is a problem that we have all been through. Do a search: Manifold, Exhaust, Header, and muffler this will give you all the info you need. Good luck and have fun with your new toy!!!||||reg||6
Z||000005||Bruce||01-03-2000||07:31 PM||||Contact your local Pontiac dealer for recall information. Give them your VIN; they can tell you if any recall work, which included fixing the cracked and leaking manifolds, was performed on your particular Fiero. The work and parts are free, so call and check.||||reg||1
Z||000006||fldevel||01-03-2000||07:50 PM||||it souns more like a valve ticking as its on every cylender and im not shure if its normal ? ||||reg||1
Z||000007||Gokart||01-03-2000||08:23 PM||||Bad injector(s)?||||reg||5
Z||000008||DRH||01-03-2000||08:27 PM||||One sound that IS normal is that you can hear the fuel injectors firing when idling. This is a ticking sound similar to valve lifters but MUCH quieter.<P>Try using a piece of pipe or even a solid piece of wood like a hammer handle. Hold one end to your ear and place the other end on each valve cover, the fuel rail, etc... When you get close to the sound you should hear the difference thru your "stethoscope".<P>The link below is a recent discussion on lifter noises. Also, you can use the Search function to search for other past threads. try words like: lifter, valve, noise, ticking, etc...<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/001674.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/001674.html</A> <BR>||||reg||1
